==English==
{{wp}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|stalkere}}, equivalent to {{af|en|stalk|-er|id2=agent noun}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈstɔːkə(ɹ)/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-stalker.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɔːkə(ɹ)|s=2}}
* {{homophones|en|stocker|aa=cot-caught}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A person who engages in [[stalk]]ing, i.e., quietly approaching animals to be hunted; a [[tracker]] or [[guide]] in hunting [[game]].
# A person who [[secretly]] [[follow]]s someone, sometimes with [[unlawful]] [[intention]]s.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2009-04-22|author=Michael Cieply|title=He’s Behind the Guffaws and the Gore|work=w:The New York Times|url=http://www.nytimes.com/2009/04/22/business/media/22culpepper.html
|passage=If the '''stalker''' thriller “Obsessed,” which opens on Friday, tops the box office, Clinton R. Culpepper will cement his reputation as Hollywood’s king of the schlockbuster.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Larry Zimmerman|title=Cheap and Easily Manipulated Video|journal=The Journal of the Kansas Bar Association|url=https://issuu.com/ksbar/docs/8704_2018_jrnl|location=Topeka, Kan.|publisher=w:Kansas Bar Association|month=April|year=2018|issn=0022-8486|page=21|passage=Ordinary people have already been face-swapped into videos for humorous or prank purposes and there is no reason to believe that abusers, harassers, '''stalkers''', and blackmailers will not soon be face-swapping victims into compromising video as part of their arsenal.}}
# Any of various [[device]]s for removing the [[stalk]] from plants during harvesting.
# Any [[bird]] that walks with a stalking motion. <!-- formerly Gradatores -->
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A kind of [[fishing net]]. <!--Webster 1913-->
# {{lb|en|horse racing}} A horse that tends to stay just behind the [[leader]]s in a race.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2024|author=Jack Adler|title=Horse Racing: An Opinion: A New Way of Seeing the Sport of Kings
|passage=If the class of the field is a '''stalker''', I'm all in in terms of evaluating his chances.}}

